  "slug": "ai-doesn-t-read-words-it-reads-tokens",
  "topic": "What is a token? How AI actually reads your words",
  "title": "AI Doesn't Read Words. It Reads Tokens.",
  "description": "Every chatbot splits your message into tokens before it reads it. Here's what a token is and why it decides your limits and costs.",
  "tags": [
   "ai",
   "chatgpt",
   "tokens",
   "llm",
   "tech explained",
   "artificial intelligence"
  ],
  "sources": [
   "OpenAI Help Center: What are tokens and how to count them"
  ],
  "scenes": [
   {
    "type": "hook",
    "heading": "AI can't read words",
    "narration": "AI chatbots don't actually read your words. They read tokens."
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "heading": "So what's a token?",
    "body": "A small chunk of text: a word, part of a word, or a symbol",
    "narration": "A token is a small chunk of text. Sometimes a whole word, sometimes part of one, sometimes just a comma."
   },
   {
    "type": "list",
    "heading": "\"unbelievable\" \u2192",
    "items": [
     "un",
     "believ",
     "able"
    ],
    "narration": "A long word like unbelievable can get split into pieces, like un, believ, and able."
   },
   {
    "type": "stat",
    "value": "\u22484",
    "label": "characters per token in English",
    "narration": "In English, one token is roughly four characters, or about three quarters of a word."
   },
   {
    "type": "bars",
    "heading": "100 English words \u2248",
    "data": [
     {
      "label": "Words",
      "value": 100
     },
     {
      "label": "Tokens",
      "value": 133
     }
    ],
    "narration": "So a hundred words is around a hundred and thirty tokens."
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "heading": "Why it matters",
    "body": "Chat limits, memory and API prices are counted in tokens",
    "narration": "And that matters, because chat limits, memory, and API pricing are all counted in tokens, not words."
   },
   {
    "type": "outro",
    "heading": "Tokens, not words",
    "narration": "Now you know how AI really reads. Follow for more tech, explained simply."
   }
  ]
 },
